{"_id":"wix-project-functionalization-of-biological-scaffolds","_type":"project","title":"Functionalization of biological scaffolds employing trophic factors released from mammalian cells","researchOrder":3,"description":[{"_type":"block","_key":"8907cb1f0c2d","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ed1216d80031","text":"Trophic factors released from mammalian cells enhance their ability to support tissue repair and regeneration. These naturally derived signalling molecules promote cell survival, proliferation and differentiation, creating a bioactive microenvironment that encourages healing while improving the scaffold's capacity to integrate with surrounding tissue.","marks":[]}]}],"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"functionalization-of-biological-scaffolds"}}
{"_id":"wix-project-neurotrophic-factors-nervous-system","_type":"project","title":"Neurotrophic factors for the differentiation and regeneration of the nervous system","researchOrder":4,"description":[{"_type":"block","_key":"e7272cd9c195","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"26fa4c5b9e6e","text":"Neurotrophic factors are essential signalling molecules that support the growth, survival and differentiation of neurons. By incorporating these bioactive molecules into regenerative therapies, we aim to enhance nerve repair, promote functional recovery and create favourable environments for nervous system regeneration following injury or disease.","marks":[]}]}],"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"neurotrophic-factors-nervous-system"}}
